WEBVTT

00:16:29.890 --> 00:16:31.566
To strengthen shared identity,

00:16:31.590 --> 00:16:33.046
Alex has created written memos

00:16:33.070 --> 00:16:35.696
to share the company's history and values.

00:16:35.720 --> 00:16:37.633
Spelling it out forced him to get clear

00:16:37.657 --> 00:16:39.306
on the team's goals and culture

00:16:39.330 --> 00:16:42.546
and helped newcomers
get up to speed from a distance.

00:16:42.570 --> 00:16:44.809
It's something they can
all revisit occasionally

00:16:44.833 --> 00:16:47.386
to remember their common
purpose and norms.

00:16:47.410 --> 00:16:49.436
And to foster shared understanding,

00:16:49.460 --> 00:16:51.945
Alex has found that it helps
to open up a little more

00:16:51.969 --> 00:16:53.216
about his home life.

00:16:53.240 --> 00:16:55.331
AC: I've found that 
it can be pretty helpful

00:16:55.331 --> 00:16:57.759
for this situation too,
even just for our coworkers,

00:16:57.783 --> 00:16:59.503
to have a little bit more awareness

00:16:59.527 --> 00:17:01.556
of what we're all doing day to day.